  "published": "2026-09-25T01:29:27.52Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "New: linqcontraband-scan --fix applies the rules' code fixes to your source files through dotnet format, then scans again and reports what is left (on Microsoft's eShop Catalog API it fixed LC008, LC023, LC042 and LC009 findings). Code-fix safety fixes from applying the fixes to real applications: LC001 no longer offers AsEnumerable() where the query must stay an IQueryable; LC005 no longer offers ThenBy when the value was sorted in another statement; LC009 keeps AsNoTracking() on the source line in multi-line queries; LC016's local-extraction fix no longer clashes with existing locals, throws or freezes a loop's clock; LC023 passes Find a key value of exactly the key type, so Find no longer throws; LC020 and LC012 fix titles say what the fix changes. LC035 no longer slows the build on long chains of optionally composed query locals.",
